  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">FAO&apos;s collaborative programme</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Global initiatives such as the Bonn Challenge and the UN Decade on Ecosystem Restoration have increased the need for policy support and technical assistance to help developing countries achieve restoration targets by 2030. At the same time, more frequent and severe wildfires driven by climate change are undermining restoration efforts, making integrated approaches that link restoration, prevention, and disaster management increasingly important.

This initiative would support the work of the Food and Agriculture Organization of the United Nations in forest landscape restoration and wildfire management, while aligning with Koreas Green ODA priorities and broader climate leadership objectives. It would also contribute to implementation of the Sustainable Development Goals and the Paris Agreement.

Key activities include contributing to ten-year restoration progress assessments, supporting preparation of next-phase restoration strategies, strengthening wildfire risk governance and early warning systems, promoting international information-sharing platforms such as the Global Fire Management Hub, and coordinating internal restoration-related cooperation mechanisms. Field-level policy advice and social/environmental safeguard support would also be provided to ensure sustainability.

Expected outcomes include stronger global forest governance, enhanced policy capacity in partner countries, wider dissemination of successful restoration models, and greater diplomatic visibility for Korea as a practical leader in climate and forest cooperation. Participation in international standards and reporting processes would also help improve the long-term global alignment of Koreas domestic forest policies.</narrative>
  </description>
